(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-refrigerant-service-decision :authorize-refrigerant-system-service-execution :proceed-with-refrigerant-system-service :override-technician-certification-requirement :bypass-technician-certification-requirement)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage" "2799007121-cloud-itonami-isco-7121-roofers-coverage" "2799007119-cloud-itonami-isco-7119-building-frame-trades-coverage" "2799007114-cloud-itonami-isco-7114-concrete-placers-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the refrigerant-system service" "proceed with the refrigerant system service" "finalize the refrigerant-system service execution decision" "finalize the refrigerant system service execution decision" "authorize the refrigerant-system service execution" "authorize the refrigerant system service execution" "override the technician-certification requirement" "override the technician certification requirement" "bypass the technician-certification requirement" "bypass the technician certification requirement")), (:adr/id 2799007127), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-service-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-service-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-service-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-service-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-service-record}, :auto #{:schedule-service-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-service-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :trades/hvac-refrigeration-service-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-service-record :schedule-service-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :technician-verified :service-account-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7127"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007127: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7127 Air Conditioning and Refrigeration Mechanics service scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7127\n-- Air Conditioning and Refrigeration Mechanics** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout, continuing the batch that already\nlanded 7111/7112/7113/7114/7119/7121.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7127\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7127\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Air Conditioning and\nRefrigeration Mechanics\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch.\nPrior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with\n`:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7127` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7127` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nAir Conditioning and Refrigeration Mechanics service pressurized\nrefrigerant systems on active job sites -- real physical-safety stakes\n(refrigerant exposure, pressurized-system hazards, electrical\nhazards). The controlling constraint for this vertical is that the\nclosed op allowlist must NEVER include any op that directly finalizes\na refrigerant-system-service-execution decision, or overrides a\ntechnician-safety-certification requirement -- those decisions must\nalways be a hard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to SERVICE\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs\nrefrigeration-system service itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders, same wave, closest domain shape: `store`/`advisor`/\n`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set,\nphysical-safety-domain closed-allowlist + always-escalate safety flag\n+ content-based scope-exclusion with a self-trip regression test) --\ncloned and read in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7127` as an OSS service\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for AC and refrigeration\nmechanics, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **HVAC Mechanic\nAdvisor ⊣ HvacMechGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **service scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct refrigeration-system-service-execution authority**\n-- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or\npropose exercising a refrigerant-system-service-execution decision, or\nany override/bypass of a technician-certification requirement. These\nare not merely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent\nfrom the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-service-record` -- service-call/parts-usage/diagnostic-status\n  data logging\n- `:schedule-service-operation` -- technician/service-call scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a refrigerant-leak/pressure-\n  anomaly/electrical-hazard concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- refrigerant/parts procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nrefrigerant-system-service-execution decision or a\ntechnician-certification-requirement override/bypass. These are\n**structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely\ngated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-refrigerant-service-decision` cannot even be proposed by\nthe reference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names five\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`hvacmech.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-refrigerant-service-decision`,\n`:authorize-refrigerant-system-service-execution`,\n`:proceed-with-refrigerant-system-service`,\n`:override-technician-certification-requirement`,\n`:bypass-technician-certification-requirement`) as defense-in-depth,\nand is verified by dedicated unit tests\n(`hvacmech.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-refrigerant-service-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-refrigerant-system-service-execution`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-refrigerant-system-service`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-technician-certification-requirement`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-bypass-technician-certification-requirement`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Technician unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered technician record, including\n   certification status (`:no-technician`). Never trusts the\n   proposal's own claim of who the technician is.\n2. **Service account unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered service account (`:no-service-account`).\n   Together with check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL\n   invariant that a technician/service-account record must be\n   independently verified/registered (including certification status)\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the five\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a\n   refrigerant-system service, or overriding/bypassing a\n   technician-certification requirement, is a second HARD, PERMANENT\n   block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on\n   content -- defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if\n   a future change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based\n   rejection still independently blocks\n   refrigerant-system-service-execution/certification-override\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a refrigerant-leak/\n  pressure-anomaly/electrical-hazard observation -- it never resolves\n  the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the\n  hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about\n  service-site safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an\n  over-threshold refrigerant/parts order is not itself unsafe, unlike\n  a refrigerant-system-service-execution or\n  technician-certification-override/bypass attempt, which is why it\n  is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural\n  absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"refrigerant\", \"certification\", \"technician\") can accidentally\nmatch inside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a\nlegitimate proposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this\nis exactly the risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a service\ncoordination actor working adjacent to refrigerant systems and\ncertified technicians necessarily discusses those concepts to do its\nscheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`hvacmech.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the\nrefrigerant-system service\", \"override the technician-certification\nrequirement\" -- matching the task's own worked example phrasing),\nnever bare nouns, and\n`hvacmech.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nservice record for technician ...\", \"scheduled service operation for\nrefrigerant diagnostic task ...\", \"... routed for certified\ntechnician review\") WITHOUT containing any of the full\nfinalization-action phrases, so the regression test is a genuine\nstress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a\nvacuous pass. Green on first run in this session -- the\nscope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never tripped during\ndevelopment. `hvacmech.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7127\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7127` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7127`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 22 tests, 47 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-refrigerant-service-decision`\n  that is merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  refrigerant-system-service-execution decision exists in the code\n  path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision this\n  severe (refrigerant exposure, pressurized-system hazards, electrical\n  hazards), the capability itself must not exist. The only op related\n  to safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the\n  need for human/certified-technician attention and never itself\n  decides, authorizes, or defers a refrigerant-system-service decision\n  for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold refrigerant/parts\n  order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft escalate\n  gate, not a hard block; only the\n  refrigerant-system-service-execution/certification-override class is\n  a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"refrigerant\"\n  \"certification\" \"technician\" \"pressure\"]`): rejected outright\n  per the fleet-known self-trip bug class described above (and\n  CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this exact task), and per the\n  explicit instruction to phrase scope-exclusion terms as\n  finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare nouns -- this actor's own\n  domain necessarily discusses refrigerant/certification/technician\n  concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would\n  risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate proposals\n  (regression-tested directly against rationale text that deliberately\n  contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `technician` and `service-account` into a single entity\n  (only checking one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity\n  provenance shape (independently-registered technician AND\n  independently-registered service account) matches the CRITICAL\n  invariant that a \"technician/service-account record must be\n  independently verified/registered (including certification status)\n  before any action\" and the established pattern from prior\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-service-record`** -- service-call/parts-usage/diagnostic-\n   status data logging only. Requires an independently registered\n   technician AND service account (`:no-technician`/\n   `:no-service-account`). Not a refrigerant-system-service-execution\n   or certification-override decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-service-operation`** -- technician/service-call\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a\n   refrigerant-system-service-execution decision (structurally absent\n   from the op's field shape; any such attempt via free text is\n   caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content check). Does not\n   authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about a specific\n   refrigerant-system service -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a refrigerant-leak/pressure-\n   anomaly/electrical-hazard concern to a human/certified technician;\n   ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the certified\n   technician reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- refrigerant/parts procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a refrigerant-system-service-\n   execution or authorization decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na refrigerant-system-service-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with\na specific refrigerant-system service) or a\ntechnician-certification-requirement override/bypass -- these\ncategories are structurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the\nclosed four-op allowlist itself (`hvacmech.governor/allowed-ops`), (b)\nfive concretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the\ngovernor-unit level (`hvacmech.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`hvacmech.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-refrigerant-service-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-refrigerant-system-service-execution`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-refrigerant-system-service`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-technician-certification-requirement`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-bypass-technician-certification-requirement`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`hvacmech.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a refrigerant-system service or override\na technician-certification requirement even via an otherwise-\nallowlisted op\n(`hvacmech.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-technician-certification`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-17"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 22, :assertions 47, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "AC and Refrigeration Service Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :technician-verification :service-account-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7127"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7127"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7127)), (:test/simulator :hvacmech.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7127 — Air Conditioning and Refrigeration Mechanics Service Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7127)))